window.CP_CONTENT = {"records":[{"id":"p00","kind":"paper","filename":"P00_introduction.md","title":"Foundations of Meaning and Knowledge Management","titleRu":"Основы управления смыслами и знаниями","artifact":"MM_A0197","revision":"MM_A0197-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"The paper proposes an operational research programme for managing transitions between a source, a representation of its content, a bounded context and the result of applying it. Its main question is when a person or an agent can reuse previously expressed content while keeping essential differences, grounds and limits under a finite budget of attention, memory and computation. The main text offers context-sufficiency boundaries, conditional properties of composition and a refutation programme. Cooking, navigation and circuit design serve synthetic analyses and limited three-book observations, not transfer to other texts. Executed appendix runs are limited and do not establish extraction quality.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0197 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0197-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P00_introduction.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>The paper proposes an operational research programme for managing transitions between a source, a representation of its content, a bounded context and the result of applying it. Its main question is when a person or an agent can reuse previously expressed content while keeping essential differences, grounds and limits under a finite budget of attention, memory and computation. The main text offers context-sufficiency boundaries, conditional properties of composition and a refutation programme. Cooking, navigation and circuit design serve synthetic analyses and limited three-book observations, not transfer to other texts. Executed appendix runs are limited and do not establish extraction quality.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>Conditional results (the F-series) hold only under their stated premises; a previously checked artifact keeps its protected properties only if the dependency manifest is complete. Basis type: proof-under-premises. No measured reuse result is claimed.</li><li>A synthetic example with three necessary parts costing 2, 2 and 3 against a budget of 5 totals 7, so the obligation cannot be met in one package. Basis type: proof-under-premises; an arithmetic example, not a measurement.</li><li>&quot;Minimal context&quot; may be claimed only with a declared option space, cost function and optimality proof. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment.</li><li>Six programme hypotheses each name a strong comparison and a refuting outcome. Basis type: hypothesis; none is tested, and no row-level status is asserted.</li><li>Appendix experiment on pre-structured material, 80 calls. Rubric A met 193 and left 7 unknown of 200 criteria; rubric B met 197 and left 3 unknown of 200. Vectors matched in 13 of 20 canonical pairs and differed in 7. Basis type: finite-test; five of five calibration controls apply to one profile only. The source MM_A5295 was NOT read by the card writer; claims resting on it keep the limited wording above.</li><li>Release cross-check by the kit authors: 13 of 14 first answers passed the narrow conditions, and in one task (T09) the first output was rejected because the register of a protected phrase changed. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment; a self-check by one assistant, not independent, and the 14 editing tasks do not test this model.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>The 12 refuting probes were editorial constructions and were not run at the initial stage; their later status is not claimed.</li><li>OCR, formulas, tables, diagrams and the 917 derived descriptions behind the three-book observations were not independently verified.</li><li>Three domains yield different defect types; they do not show transfer to other texts or professions.</li><li>Universality of the general model is not proved.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is OPEN. Independent semantic review of this text has NOT been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>The research crosswalk is integrated but is a one-assistant self-check by the kit authors, not independent confirmation.</li><li>Not integrated and still missing: the NAV reports, the TIM reports, MM_OBLIGATIONS_20261030 together with the previous-stage report, the runs behind section 7 of the knowledge-admission amendment (MM_KA0004), and the items ING-01 to ING-08.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>The Russian full text is the terminology edition of 2026-11-03 (front matter and links aside). Where the editorial card corrects the status wording of its abstract (executed appendix results that the abstract understates), this page follows the corrected, evidence-bound wording and says so here. The Russian text is published without the card corrections, so its abstract may differ from this page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/P00_introduction.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P00_introduction.md","image":"knowledge-prism.webp","source_sha256":"33aed0c8bbe8c805944272fc33c58344537591694fc50e4ee42912ff4eb3fdd2"},{"id":"p01","kind":"paper","filename":"P01_semantic_objects_and_extraction.md","title":"Semantic Objects, Sources and Verifiable Extraction","titleRu":"Смысловые объекты, источники и проверяемое извлечение","artifact":"MM_A0198","revision":"MM_A0198-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"The paper proposes a profile of the semantic object (`MeaningObject`) and a protocol for verifiable extraction. The profile ties content to specific source editions, operator scopes, composite grounds, alternative readings and separate assessments. The central hypothesis is that such binding can reduce reuse errors in declared task classes; it admits a negative result, since for plain retrieval detailed markup may cost more than it helps. The main edition prepared a model, a protocol, limited example records and a test design, and ran no automatic extraction on full books. The appendix keeps limited executed slices over structured material, which do not establish extraction from free text.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0198 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0198-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P01_semantic_objects_and_extraction.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>The paper proposes a profile of the semantic object (<code>MeaningObject</code>) and a protocol for verifiable extraction. The profile ties content to specific source editions, operator scopes, composite grounds, alternative readings and separate assessments. The central hypothesis is that such binding can reduce reuse errors in declared task classes; it admits a negative result, since for plain retrieval detailed markup may cost more than it helps. The main edition prepared a model, a protocol, limited example records and a test design, and ran no automatic extraction on full books. The appendix keeps limited executed slices over structured material, which do not establish extraction from free text.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>The example registry holds 24 semantic objects in 101 local records. Basis type: not-a-claim; these are counts of development artefacts, not extraction quality, and no extraction pipeline was run on them.</li><li>The closure of a finite pinned graph reaches a fixed point and is the least closure. Basis type: proof-under-premises (finite graph, given roots and required edges). A missed legend stays missed.</li><li>The other local formal properties are structural consequences of the chosen discipline. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment, not proved novelty.</li><li>The central hypothesis and the plan H01-H08 each have refuting observations. Basis type: hypothesis; none confirmed.</li><li>Appendix slices on structured input exposed first failures that stay visible: seven assessment records of variant B had incompatible <code>target.scope</code> and top-level <code>scope</code>; four initial <code>unknown</code> values for variant A were attributed to the assessor and were not rewritten to <code>met</code>; in one earlier round a required <code>source_conditions</code> field was missing. Basis type: finite-test; structured inputs only.</li><li>The release cross-check bound rules to 124 exact byte selectors, which include one block reuse (123 distinct blocks). Basis type: authors-domain-assessment; this is naming and byte binding, not extraction quality. The crosswalk phrase about 40 author semantic checks is NOT VERIFIED and is not used.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>No production quality, throughput, universal text/image equivalence or accuracy on real books is claimed.</li><li>A structural validator checks pinned references and declared fields, not whether an image was read correctly.</li><li>No real pairs of OCR and verified transcription exist for the three books; OCR accuracy against the original PDF was not measured.</li><li>No cost measurement compares annotation with reading the source.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is OPEN. Independent semantic review of this text has NOT been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>The sources MM_A0275, MM_A0263 and MM_A0274 (behind the registry counts) and the gap map MM_A5300 (behind the appendix slices) were NOT read by the card writer; claims resting on them keep the limited wording above.</li><li>The research crosswalk is integrated but is a one-assistant self-check by the kit authors, not independent confirmation.</li><li>Not integrated and still missing: the NAV reports, the TIM reports, MM_OBLIGATIONS_20261030 together with the previous-stage report, the runs behind section 7 of the knowledge-admission amendment (MM_KA0004), and the items ING-01 to ING-08.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>The Russian full text is the terminology edition of 2026-11-03 (front matter and links aside). Where the editorial card corrects the status wording of its abstract (executed appendix slices that a &quot;not run&quot; statement would understate), this page follows the corrected, evidence-bound wording and says so here. The Russian text is published without the card corrections, so its abstract may differ from this page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/P01_semantic_objects_and_extraction.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P01_semantic_objects_and_extraction.md","image":"knowledge-landscape.webp","source_sha256":"9573308454e240cddc36f59890e72258f6de782bb0422dcaf4e6d297bf772223"},{"id":"p02","kind":"paper","filename":"P02_context_and_applicability.md","title":"Context, Depth and Conditions of Applicability","titleRu":"Контекст, глубина и условия применимости","artifact":"MM_A0199","revision":"MM_A0199-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"The paper proposes a model in which extracted content, the conditions for understanding it and the conditions of a new application are addressed separately. For each task a finite set of requirements is formed, and applicability is judged against knowledge editions, contexts, the addressee, the method and available grounds. The main edition gives definitions, conditional properties and a test plan and ran no three-book tests; the appendix keeps later limited runs, including a negative result.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0199 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0199-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P02_context_and_applicability.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>The paper proposes a model in which extracted content, the conditions for understanding it and the conditions of a new application are addressed separately. For each task a finite set of requirements is formed, and applicability is judged against knowledge editions, contexts, the addressee, the method and available grounds. The main edition gives definitions, conditional properties and a test plan and ran no three-book tests; the appendix keeps later limited runs, including a negative result.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>Naive deduplication fails in illustrated cases: a record for 4 servings and one for 6 should not merge, and two books copying one source are not two independent witnesses. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment; examples are illustrative, not measured.</li><li>Conditional properties CP01-CP08 separate logical consequences of definitions from empirical hypotheses; an unknown value does not pass a mandatory barrier. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment; the per-property proofs in MM_A0301 were NOT read by the card writer.</li><li>Applicability improves for concrete tasks at a justified cost of explicit structure. Basis type: hypothesis; nothing beyond illustrated is claimed.</li><li>The bounded executable profile reports 103 checks passed with no errors. Basis type: finite-test; declared operations and author examples only, groups not independent experiments.</li><li>Appendix protocol for addressed revision: 30 cases from three books, two implementations per case, 60 executions matching expected outcomes. Basis type: finite-test over a finite area; 36 assessments with unresolved mapping and 12 with an unknown contract condition are intended results; the revision results link was NOT read by the card writer.</li><li>Negative result: a simple alternative with the same data and conditions gave the same answers in all 30 pairs. Basis type: finite-test.</li><li>A release cross-check by the kit authors shows separate rule conditions on tasks T02, T05, T08 and T12-T14. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment; a self-check by one assistant, with genres and hidden contexts not exhausted. The per-task results of T08, T13 and T14 beyond the one-line examples are NOT VERIFIED.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>Hidden premises of arbitrary text are not detected; subject cases and three-book page processing remain not executed.</li><li>A positive structural validation is not proof of correct understanding.</li><li>Seven assessment records had <code>target.scope</code> inconsistent with the top-level <code>scope</code>, so no single verified applicability area was defined.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is OPEN. Independent semantic review of this text has NOT been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>The executed protocol MM_A5295 was NOT read by the card writer; claims resting on it keep the limited wording above.</li><li>The research crosswalk is integrated but is a one-assistant self-check by the kit authors, not independent confirmation.</li><li>A later engineering amendment (passports that always show conditions and bounds) is an interface change that does not alter the truth of knowledge; the report behind it was not checked in this edition.</li><li>Not integrated and still missing: the NAV reports, the TIM reports, MM_OBLIGATIONS_20261030 together with the previous-stage report, the runs behind section 7 of the knowledge-admission amendment (MM_KA0004), and the items ING-01 to ING-08.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>The Russian full text is the terminology edition of 2026-11-03 (front matter and links aside). Where the editorial card corrects the status wording of its abstract (an unscoped &quot;not tested on three books&quot; replaced by a scoped statement), this page follows the corrected, evidence-bound wording and says so here. The Russian text is published without the card corrections, so its abstract may differ from this page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/P02_context_and_applicability.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P02_context_and_applicability.md","image":"knowledge-dialogue.webp","source_sha256":"7568ab3eca9b34985afbaeae8528a66437e860a41295e18759e2df1401cbe2c7"},{"id":"p03","kind":"paper","filename":"P03_transformations_and_transfer.md","title":"Transformations, Composition and Bounded Transfer","titleRu":"Преобразования, композиция и ограниченный перенос","artifact":"MM_A0200","revision":"MM_A0200-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"Reusing knowledge requires transformations: normalisation, reduction, joining sources, inference, parametrisation and transfer to a new situation. The paper proposes a transition contract linking input editions, the permitted effect, preconditions, postconditions, protected properties, assumptions, losses and the actual output. Geometric similarity only selects candidates. Conditional properties are arguments under explicit premises, and hypotheses about the benefit of the profile are untested; the appendix keeps limited executed experiments that do not confirm them. It does not claim a universal computable algebra of human meaning.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0200 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0200-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P03_transformations_and_transfer.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>Reusing knowledge requires transformations: normalisation, reduction, joining sources, inference, parametrisation and transfer to a new situation. The paper proposes a transition contract linking input editions, the permitted effect, preconditions, postconditions, protected properties, assumptions, losses and the actual output. Geometric similarity only selects candidates. Conditional properties are arguments under explicit premises, and hypotheses about the benefit of the profile are untested; the appendix keeps limited executed experiments that do not confirm them. It does not claim a universal computable algebra of human meaning.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>The architecture has three levels (content, operation, execution); substituting one for another produces false promises, since a correct schema does not guarantee correct inference. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment; a design stance, not a theorem.</li><li>Ten conditional properties CP01-CP10 are arguments under explicit premises, not proofs and not empirical results. A worked three-step chain shows that a dropped condition is not restored by an old report. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment.</li><li>Four hypotheses need empirical evaluation. Basis type: hypothesis; the appendix does not establish them.</li><li>Appendix logs for the three books hold 100 culinary, 41 automatic and 28 navigation operations, all marked <code>auto_applied_unreviewed</code>. The first literal mapping linked 100 of 100, 41 of 41 and only 21 of 28; a later mapping reproduced and reversed all 28, and the failed first attempt is kept. Basis type: finite-test.</li><li>Vectors matched in 13 of 20 canonical pairs, which is not evidence that the carriers are equivalent; 7 of 20 differed. Basis type: finite-test.</li><li>A release cross-check by the kit authors tested idempotence and join for skill-dependency closure on all 4096 subsets of 12 skills. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment; a self-check by one assistant, covering finite-traversal laws, not an algebra of meaning, with geometry not implemented.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>The navigation readable file did not reproduce whole, and three captions fell into alt-text; reversing an operation over one block is not restoring the full artifact.</li><li>The finite profile does not test recognition of arbitrary phrases, implicit domain models or visual understanding. No execution report of it was read.</li><li>Practical confirmation needs permitted pages of three books, fixed OCR/VLM versions and independent labelling; counts of documents are not a measure of truth.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is OPEN. Independent semantic review of this text has NOT been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>The sources MM_A5295, MM_A10271 (mapping history) and MM_A5300 (gap plan) were NOT read by the card writer; claims resting on them keep the limited wording above.</li><li>The research crosswalk is integrated but is a one-assistant self-check by the kit authors, not independent confirmation.</li><li>A later engineering amendment separates migration of representation paths from semantic transformation; it is a layout change, and the report behind it was not checked.</li><li>Not integrated and still missing: the NAV reports, the TIM reports, MM_OBLIGATIONS_20261030 together with the previous-stage report, the runs behind section 7 of the knowledge-admission amendment (MM_KA0004), and the items ING-01 to ING-08.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>The Russian full text is the terminology edition of 2026-11-03 (front matter and links aside). Where the editorial card corrects the status wording of its abstract (appendix experiments that an unscoped &quot;not tested&quot; would understate), this page follows the corrected, evidence-bound wording and says so here. The Russian text is published without the card corrections, so its abstract may differ from this page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/P03_transformations_and_transfer.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P03_transformations_and_transfer.md","image":"knowledge-prism.webp","source_sha256":"85d3ae0d0b6fb8e7818e6650e637c2a6a635defe4ca136b6f0b468a58987b7ad"},{"id":"p04","kind":"paper","filename":"P04_query_retrieval_and_coverage.md","title":"Query, Retrieval and Verifiable Coverage","titleRu":"Запрос, извлечение и проверяемое покрытие","artifact":"MM_A0201","revision":"MM_A0201-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"The paper proposes a profile for moving from a human or agent query to a bounded answer set with checkable grounds. It separates relevance, support, search completeness and applicability. It links a query plan (`QueryPlan`), a candidate set, three separately addressed coverage reports (`CoverageReport`), pinned sources and stop rules. It allows a useful partial answer and does not treat \"nothing found\" as \"nothing known\". Its properties hold only under explicit premises: a finite domain, a query parsed in advance, and author-marked metadata. Only an authored finite model was executed; no real-book search has been run.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0201 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0201-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P04_query_retrieval_and_coverage.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>The paper proposes a profile for moving from a human or agent query to a bounded answer set with checkable grounds. It separates relevance, support, search completeness and applicability. It links a query plan (<code>QueryPlan</code>), a candidate set, three separately addressed coverage reports (<code>CoverageReport</code>), pinned sources and stop rules. It allows a useful partial answer and does not treat &quot;nothing found&quot; as &quot;nothing known&quot;. Its properties hold only under explicit premises: a finite domain, a query parsed in advance, and author-marked metadata. Only an authored finite model was executed; no real-book search has been run.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>The three coverage reports are addressed independently. Basis type: finite-test. Scope: the authored finite model, 97 checks, 97 passed. Five finite enumerations cover 352 configurations, which is not 352 independent experiments.</li><li>A negative conclusion is allowed only for an explicitly finite domain with current pins, a complete survey and all evaluations negative. Basis type: proof-under-premises. It does not extend to missed pages, hidden data, OCR errors or subject interpretation. Linked MM_A0372 was NOT read.</li><li>A second agent wrote 12 minimal API probes and first found 2 defects: an 8-byte PNG signature accepted as a sufficient image, and an irrelevant fact&#x27;s origin entering the evidence groups. After fixes, 11 probes passed and 1 passed with a limitation. Basis type: finite-test. Not a human review, not an independent implementation.</li><li>An engineering cross-check of the RU10 release maps all 427 recognised pages; the selected rule supports are 123 blocks on 69 pages out of 2746 blocks, which is not a share of the book&#x27;s meanings. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment. It is a one-assistant self-check by the kit authors, not independent confirmation. That agents select ready rules and skills is NOT VERIFIED: a design statement, no run record.</li><li>A budget stop issues no completeness certificate (the operational profile MM_A0383 was linked, NOT read), and deduplicated copies are not independent evidence (uniqueness is declared, not statistically shown). Basis type for both: authors-domain-assessment; design rules, not measured on real retrieval.</li><li>Hypotheses H12-01 to H12-08 each have a strong alternative and a revision condition. Basis type: hypothesis; no results.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>No real corpus search, no comparison with BM25, dense or hybrid retrieval on independent labels, and no cost measurement.</li><li>36 system scenarios and 9 sequential walkthroughs were planned and not executed.</li><li>Query recognition, server-side vector search, OCR/VLM and products were not run; automatic semantic search and recall over the whole book are not assessed.</li><li>A structural SQL-like query over normalised data may solve a task more simply; then no advantage is claimed.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>The research synthesis crosswalk is integrated only as authors-domain-assessment. A proposed addendum on separating file, source, meaning and index coverage has no executed result.</li><li>Not integrated and still missing: the NAV reports, the TIM reports, MM_OBLIGATIONS_20261030 together with the previous-stage report, the runs behind section 7 of the knowledge-admission amendment (MM_KA0004), and the items ING-01 to ING-08.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>The Russian full text is the terminology edition of 2026-11-03 (front matter and links aside). Its abstract states the status but not the executed basis; this page follows the corrected, evidence-bound wording of the round-two editorial card. The Russian text is published without the card corrections, so its abstract may differ from this page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/P04_query_retrieval_and_coverage.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P04_query_retrieval_and_coverage.md","image":"knowledge-landscape.webp","source_sha256":"bedfb67e1938c0f64e6348deb04b861d6948b2ec57a227b9c8e54d35a6b272a6"},{"id":"p05","kind":"paper","filename":"P05_budgeted_context_composition.md","title":"Context Composition under a Limited Budget","titleRu":"Составление контекста при ограниченном бюджете","artifact":"MM_A0202","revision":"MM_A0202-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"The paper studies how to compose a context from a fixed set of candidates under limited resources. It proposes a conditional model in which requirements, joint grounds, mandatory dependencies, permitted transformations and the actual representation form one object of verification. The main result is a specification, conditional properties, counter-models, a finite executable model and a comparison plan. Executed: 101 finite checks and 17 API probes. Empirical advantage on real books, people, models or products is not established.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0202 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0202-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P05_budgeted_context_composition.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>The paper studies how to compose a context from a fixed set of candidates under limited resources. It proposes a conditional model in which requirements, joint grounds, mandatory dependencies, permitted transformations and the actual representation form one object of verification. The main result is a specification, conditional properties, counter-models, a finite executable model and a comparison plan. Executed: 101 finite checks and 17 API probes. Empirical advantage on real books, people, models or products is not established.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>Ranking does not settle sufficiency: two ingredients from different dishes do not meet a one-dish condition. Basis type: finite-test, authored vectors; real-query failure rates are not measured.</li><li>The finite check had 101 checks: 24 authored vectors, 68 negative controls, 5 enumerations over 576 configurations (not independent experiments), 2 constructed counter-models and 2 boundary checks. Basis type: finite-test. Separately, 17 API probes were written without the authored vectors or expected answers; the first run gave 13 pass and 4 findings, the repeat on the same inputs 17 passes. Authorship separation within one session is not an independent replication.</li><li>A special case (cover requirements with at most k independent unit-cost packages) contains SET COVER and is NP-hard. A scheme and a legend may each be insufficient yet together close a requirement. Basis type for both: proof-under-premises; hardness of real queries and effect frequency are not established.</li><li>A closure lemma (an addendum, not in the Russian text): the smallest mandatory closure in a finite graph is the fixed point of adding needed vertices. Basis type: proof-under-premises (fixed vertices, ALL-type edges, complete edges). A machine check enumerated all 512 graphs on three vertices; beyond that the lemma rests on the written proof.</li><li>An engineering cross-check of the RU10 release: a structural validator rejects a control omission of a critical condition (selftest, K08-condition-1). Basis type: authors-domain-assessment (one-assistant self-check by the kit authors, not independent). Minimality, optimality and token reduction are not established; the meaning of the crosswalk&#x27;s &quot;R01 exposes the whole core&quot; is NOT VERIFIED.</li><li>Eight hypotheses H13 have status <code>empirical_result_absent</code>. Basis type: hypothesis; no results.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>The unit is UTF-8 bytes of deterministic JSON, not model tokens, human reading or time under load.</li><li>Exact selection covers at most 16 given representations, canonical order only.</li><li>Cited external submodular-optimisation theorems are quoted with premises, not proved here and not verified by the writer.</li><li>36 system scenarios and 9 sequential walkthroughs were not executed; sample size, effects and thresholds are unjustified, and causal usefulness is not established.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>An ALL/ANY alternatives proposal is an unexecuted hypothesis.</li><li>NOT read by the card writer: MM_A0401, MM_A0402 (proofs), MM_A0406 (S05), the closure-lemma test side (CLOSURE_LAWS.json); claims resting on them keep the card&#x27;s limited wording.</li><li>Not integrated and still missing: the NAV reports, the TIM reports, MM_OBLIGATIONS_20261030 together with the previous-stage report, the runs behind section 7 of the knowledge-admission amendment (MM_KA0004), and the items ING-01 to ING-08.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>The Russian full text is the terminology edition of 2026-11-03 (front matter and links aside). This page follows the card&#x27;s evidence-bound wording and drops &quot;independent&quot; for the probe separation. The Russian text is published without the card corrections, so its abstract may differ from this page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/P05_budgeted_context_composition.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P05_budgeted_context_composition.md","image":"knowledge-dialogue.webp","source_sha256":"57095f269a94b793f46cc0159613dba2ebaa474fd4ee1f6daf31c1cc4d65e54a"},{"id":"p06","kind":"paper","filename":"P06_dialogue_and_learning.md","title":"Dialogue, Learning and Alignment of Understanding","titleRu":"Диалог, обучение и согласование понимания","artifact":"MM_A0203","revision":"MM_A0203-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"The paper offers a specification and a limited transition profile over structured dialogue events. It assesses separately how an utterance is interpreted, whether a state transition is admissible, and whether the reply was useful. Interpretation, the subject registry and subject-verification data come from outside the profile. Free-language understanding, real external effects and training of model weights are not claimed. The executed result is a local pilot on fictional, deliberately constructed episodes, without human participants. It matched declared expectations in 31 of 32 episodes on the first run, and a simple baseline reached the same counts on the shared subset, so no advantage was observed.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0203 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0203-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P06_dialogue_and_learning.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>The paper offers a specification and a limited transition profile over structured dialogue events. It assesses separately how an utterance is interpreted, whether a state transition is admissible, and whether the reply was useful. Interpretation, the subject registry and subject-verification data come from outside the profile. Free-language understanding, real external effects and training of model weights are not claimed. The executed result is a local pilot on fictional, deliberately constructed episodes, without human participants. It matched declared expectations in 31 of 32 episodes on the first run, and a simple baseline reached the same counts on the shared subset, so no advantage was observed.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>Pilot: 31 of 32 episodes (171 of 172 assertions) matched expectations; the single mismatch concerned the diagnostic status of applying not-yet-accepted memory. After one minimal fix, a repeat gave 32/32 and 172/172, which is a known-set regression, not new independent confirmation. A simple baseline gave the same 6/6 useful results and 0/4 forbidden admissions on the shared subset. Basis type: finite-test. The 172 assertions are not 172 dialogues, and the agent that built the control set also prepared the interpretation.</li><li>The reducer accepted 2 of 2 semantically false &quot;trusted&quot; annotations, in both runs. Basis type: finite-test. Structural guarantees do not confirm meaning.</li><li>The state key is user, task and branch inside one tenant, with owner and roles taken from an external trusted registry. Basis type: finite-test, on the 32 pilot episodes; the registry does not authenticate a user; the episode list was NOT read by the card writer.</li><li>Understanding, acceptance, intent, support, authority and learning are assessment roles, not a trust scale, and fourteen conditional properties give a checkable argument about the transition design. Basis type for both: authors-domain-assessment; not a proof, not machine verification; the motivating literature (MM_A0714) was NOT read and is NOT VERIFIED.</li><li>Engineering cross-check of the RU10 release: two single-step examples (T13 and T14) ask targeted questions when inputs are missing, without invented content. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment. They are self-assessed fixtures, not dialogue sessions, with no blind reviewer or matched baseline; a one-assistant self-check by the kit authors, not independent. The crosswalk phrase about explaining edits is NOT VERIFIED.</li><li>Showing known, observed and verified states separately may reduce misreading of <code>unknown</code> as a negative judgement of a person. Basis type: hypothesis; no human study.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>No human participants: understanding, learning effect, skill transfer and interface convenience were not measured.</li><li>Model weights are not trained, and <code>competence=not_established</code> is kept.</li><li>Zero forbidden admissions on the main set does not mean no semantic errors on arbitrary replies.</li><li>Concurrent updates and external storage transactions are outside the model.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>A proposal that remarks become addressable fix tasks is an unexecuted hypothesis.</li><li>Not integrated and still missing: the NAV reports, the TIM reports, MM_OBLIGATIONS_20261030 together with the previous-stage report, the runs behind section 7 of the knowledge-admission amendment (MM_KA0004), and the items ING-01 to ING-08.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>The Russian full text is the terminology edition of 2026-11-03 (front matter and links aside). It has no abstract section; the card proposes one, and the Abstract above rests on that proposal. The Russian text is published without the card corrections, so its abstract may differ from this page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/P06_dialogue_and_learning.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P06_dialogue_and_learning.md","image":"knowledge-dialogue.webp","source_sha256":"d8ac6d6ed38ca15ac7a2ef3095e418dfb48e3f75ab71e780380701d2ee76a6ae"},{"id":"p07","kind":"paper","filename":"P07_reasoning_and_evidence.md","title":"Reasoning, Justification and Revision of Conclusions","titleRu":"Рассуждение, обоснование и пересмотр выводов","artifact":"MM_A0204","revision":"MM_A0204-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"The paper concerns revising a stored conclusion when one of its premises changes. Its central counterexample: a mark \"source changed\" does not show that a claim is false, since the old justification may be outdated, other support may remain, an opposite premise may be confirmed, or data may be insufficient. The executable profile covers structured claims and declared rules only. A check on real acquired sources has its own scope and does not measure OCR quality, language understanding or industrial agents. The executed basis is an authored finite check on three public documents.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0204 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0204-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P07_reasoning_and_evidence.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>The paper concerns revising a stored conclusion when one of its premises changes. Its central counterexample: a mark &quot;source changed&quot; does not show that a claim is false, since the old justification may be outdated, other support may remain, an opposite premise may be confirmed, or data may be insufficient. The executable profile covers structured claims and declared rules only. A check on real acquired sources has its own scope and does not measure OCR quality, language understanding or industrial agents. The executed basis is an authored finite check on three public documents.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>On three public documents (NIST, NOAA, and one recipe fragment of a USDA collection), development ran 73/73. The first separately written set (R0) gave 22/24 (positive decisions 7/8). After two fixes the repeat (R1) gave 24/24 and 8/8, then 75/75 after later changes. Basis type: finite-test. R1 is a known-set regression, not new independent confirmation; 24 variants are not 24 independent sources.</li><li>The bare engine admitted 2 of 2 wrongly trusted markup cases; the source-admission guard rejected 2 of 2. On 12 shared cases a simple direct baseline admitted 7/7 positive candidates (first model 6/7, corrected 7/7); superiority is not established. Basis type: finite-test.</li><li>Reuse bound to the source head worked in 2 of 2 cases; consequences of a changed premise are not proven. Absence of known proof yields <code>unknown</code> or a limited negative, not negation; first failure: <code>current</code> for a receipt without read target evidence became <code>unknown</code>. Alternative grounds are kept separately; completeness of automatically found ones is unproven. Basis type: finite-test.</li><li>Acyclicity is a representation property, not truth of data; finite-graph checkability is a conditional argument with examples, not a machine proof. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment.</li><li>Engineering cross-check of the RU10 release: change grounds are recorded in self-assessments of 14 cases; checking single cases found three distinct defects in the saved producer-side graph (lost polarity and scope, a wrong negation flag, example columns read as a definition). Basis type: authors-domain-assessment. A one-assistant self-check by the kit authors, not independent; the three findings are not an error rate and none became working rules.</li><li>Correct choice of dependency type is the next object of refutation: a flawless closure over misclassified relations is possible. Basis type: hypothesis.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>No control case has reference outcome <code>refuted</code>, so sensitivity to genuine refutation is not measured.</li><li>All six OCR quality reports of a later pilot carry CER/WER <code>null</code>: no benchmark ran, not zero error.</li><li>Origin groups are declared attribution, not statistical independence; one-team test order is not external replication.</li><li>Evaluation covers given candidates, not generation of answers.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>A proposed addendum (a technical pass creates no support) is a hypothesis awaiting executed results.</li><li>Not integrated and still missing: the NAV reports, the TIM reports, MM_OBLIGATIONS_20261030 together with the previous-stage report, the runs behind section 7 of the knowledge-admission amendment (MM_KA0004), and the items ING-01 to ING-08.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>The Russian full text is the terminology edition of 2026-11-03 (front matter, links aside). It has no abstract section; this Abstract rests on the opening section plus the card&#x27;s proposal. The Russian text is published without the card corrections, so its abstract may differ from this page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/P07_reasoning_and_evidence.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P07_reasoning_and_evidence.md","image":"knowledge-landscape.webp","source_sha256":"1e8bdb49dc2ca64452ca0c70bb5c74aab9d5c17ed196489cbffd8c0dfd7a54cc"},{"id":"p08","kind":"paper","filename":"P08_documents_and_memory.md","title":"Documents, Representations and Long-Term Memory","titleRu":"Документы, представления и долговременная память","artifact":"MM_A0205","revision":"MM_A0205-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"The paper treats a document as a defined representation of knowledge for a purpose, audience and genre, and asks what editing and memory must preserve: conditions of applicability, dependent paragraphs, source locators and current permission to use. It separates three levels of result: a specification of obligations, a finite local execution over trusted, already interpreted units, and future empirical work. The execution checks declared dependencies, current admission and the actual Markdown/JSON projection. It does not check whether a quotation matches its primary source or whether the markup is true.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0205 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0205-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P08_documents_and_memory.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>The paper treats a document as a defined representation of knowledge for a purpose, audience and genre, and asks what editing and memory must preserve: conditions of applicability, dependent paragraphs, source locators and current permission to use. It separates three levels of result: a specification of obligations, a finite local execution over trusted, already interpreted units, and future empirical work. The execution checks declared dependencies, current admission and the actual Markdown/JSON projection. It does not check whether a quotation matches its primary source or whether the markup is true.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>Quotation fidelity, factual truth, completeness and current validity are independent coordinates, not in the statistical sense. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment.</li><li>Checking only an edited paragraph gives false acceptance when a stale conclusion remains elsewhere. The whole selected set, conflicts and delivered projection must be checked. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment.</li><li>Restoring a snapshot returns data but does not restore permissions, if current state is not overwritten. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment (conditional, not a proof).</li><li>The last verification layer processed 917 records in three books, with two passes of 19,305 field checks and no field violations. Basis type: finite-test, local and deterministic. The repeated materialisation does not create 1,834 independent semantic observations. A control outcome of 15/16 is kept together with a separate correction; its meaning is NOT VERIFIED beyond the edition text.</li><li>First failures stay visible. In an early load attempt, consistency of the later SQLite readback was not confirmed. A local replay of 28 ledger operations on a navigation book did not reproduce the full readable file, and three alt-text copies also changed. A late failure after the CURRENT pointer replacement, before fsync completed, was also found. Basis type: finite-test, one book each.</li><li>The RU10 release cross-check: 13 of 14 first answers passed the narrow conditions, and the T09 rejection is kept with a separate corrected attempt. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment, a one-assistant self-check.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>Nothing is established about real books, reader comprehension, or a production permission mechanism.</li><li>Restoration is logical only, not physical erasure or recovery of external copies.</li><li>Four hypotheses (fewer contradictions, fewer misapplied caveats, cheaper partial updates, fewer outdated decisions) are planned, not tested; external studies were not replicated.</li><li>Open: automatic dependency discovery, free paraphrase, locator transfer after OCR, long-term service operation.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>Not integrated and still missing: the NAV reports, the TIM reports, MM_OBLIGATIONS_20261030 together with the previous-stage report, the runs behind section 7 of the knowledge-admission amendment (MM_KA0004), and the items ING-01 to ING-08.</li><li>The crosswalk content is a one-assistant self-check, not independent confirmation; its receipt-overwrite ban is NOT VERIFIED.</li><li>NOT read by the card writer: the I25 run reports (MM_A0754), source review (MM_A0762), property register (MM_A0755) and R44 reports (MM_A13315). Figures come from the appendix text; claims resting on these keep the limited wording above. A later artifact-layout amendment is not merged.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>The Russian full text is the terminology edition of 2026-11-03 (front matter, links aside). It has no abstract section, so this page uses the abstract proposed in the editorial review and follows its evidence-bound wording. The Russian text is published without the card corrections, so its abstract may differ from this page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/P08_documents_and_memory.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P08_documents_and_memory.md","image":"knowledge-dialogue.webp","source_sha256":"f259a9659e6000205d11b2090d15b987d3e423d90b223c500c33f18869103cfe"},{"id":"p09","kind":"paper","filename":"P09_work_roles_skills_and_kc.md","title":"Knowledge Contract v3: Synthesis of the General Model and a Professional Profile","titleRu":"Контракт знаний v3: синтез общей модели и профессиональный профиль","artifact":"MM_A0206","revision":"MM_A0206-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"The paper proposes a general Knowledge Contract (KC) v3 interface linking addressable content to purpose, conditions, grounds, dependencies and rules of use. Nine core groups are extended by six selective profiles. The professional profile separates a unit of work (`WorkItem`), role (`Role`), skill description (`Skill`), solution scheme (`Blueprint`), executor capability, current authority, attempt and evidence. For a bounded interchange format the authors implemented a JSON Schema, consistency checks, consumer compatibility, current-use evaluation and a v2 subset migration. It is finite and works on trusted, interpreted JSON input.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0206 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0206-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P09_work_roles_skills_and_kc.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>The paper proposes a general Knowledge Contract (KC) v3 interface linking addressable content to purpose, conditions, grounds, dependencies and rules of use. Nine core groups are extended by six selective profiles. The professional profile separates a unit of work (<code>WorkItem</code>), role (<code>Role</code>), skill description (<code>Skill</code>), solution scheme (<code>Blueprint</code>), executor capability, current authority, attempt and evidence. For a bounded interchange format the authors implemented a JSON Schema, consistency checks, consumer compatibility, current-use evaluation and a v2 subset migration. It is finite and works on trusted, interpreted JSON input.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>The authors&#x27; first run passed 35/35 contract scenarios. A control set passed 26/26. Basis type: finite-test. The control set was composed by a separate agent of the same session from the public interface; it is not external verification. One control intent is unmapped and five are partly mapped; the gap list after that count was NOT read by the card writer.</li><li>Two authors&#x27; cases and four control cases with false trusted inputs were accepted. They show the model boundary, outside the main figure. Basis type: finite-test.</li><li>A diagnostic ablation without part of the checks scored 3/9 against 9/9; it is not a strong baseline. An exploratory comparison with a strong plain form, prepared after first results were disclosed, scored 9/9 on both sides; its evidence file (MM_A0790) was NOT read. Basis type: finite-test.</li><li>A strong plain alternative gave the same result in 30 targeted-revision pairs (negative). Basis type: finite-test; the underlying report was not read.</li><li>The distinctions among role, skill description, solution scheme, capability and authority are definitions. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment.</li><li>RU10 cross-check, by the kit authors and one assistant: 107 entries of the r1 delivery use valid AKP forms. The r2 set has 110 entries, after three competence descriptions were added. In r1, 14 of 14 retained results were re-mapped to the contract. An empty <code>Blueprint</code> list in the first adapter was fixed. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment.</li><li>The central proposal is a hypothesis; H01-H04 are planned, not executed. Basis type: hypothesis.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>Source markup correctness and external authority are not established by the validator.</li><li>Speed, cost and minimality of groups and profiles are not measured.</li><li>The check records no revision or hash of the contract.</li><li>Authors, composer and assessors share one session.</li><li>Migration covers one historical shape; semantic equivalence stays <code>not_established</code> (the migration report MM_A0804 not read; the claim rests on the read MM_A0810).</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>Not integrated and still missing: the NAV reports, the TIM reports, MM_OBLIGATIONS_20261030 together with the previous-stage report, the runs behind section 7 of the knowledge-admission amendment (MM_KA0004), and the items ING-01 to ING-08.</li><li>The crosswalk content is a one-assistant self-check, not independent confirmation.</li><li>Held: the edition says another team member composed the control set, the review says an agent of the same session (this page follows the review); the amendment speaks of seven profiles, the edition lists six.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>The Russian full text is the terminology edition of 2026-11-03 (front matter, links aside). Its abstract understates executed results; this page follows the corrected wording of the editorial review. The Russian text is published without the card corrections, so its abstract may differ from this page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/P09_work_roles_skills_and_kc.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P09_work_roles_skills_and_kc.md","image":"knowledge-landscape.webp","source_sha256":"1907861fb674ff0e99057707b81165ad98f568cda3a8e1e6c3fc5cac5044048a"},{"id":"p10","kind":"paper","filename":"P10_revision_and_canon.md","title":"Revision of Knowledge, Versions and Acceptance of Norms","titleRu":"Пересмотр знания, версии и принятие норм","artifact":"MM_A0207","revision":"MM_A0207-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"The paper sets rules for changing knowledge, its grounds, norms and chosen representations, connecting them with history, publication and current admission. A finite revision model passed 73 checks with fixed inputs (0 failed); three model defects were found and fixed during preparation. In one observation of a file operation, a separate copy failed finalisation in a previous update (301 of 302 save operations succeeded) and the service gave no cause; the full archive still matched the canonical sources (348 of 348 hashes). No real distributed backend, authentication, books or classifier were used, and 36 subject and load setups remain planned and not executed. Superiority over simply replacing the last record is not shown.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0207 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0207-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P10_revision_and_canon.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>The paper sets rules for changing knowledge, its grounds, norms and chosen representations, connecting them with history, publication and current admission. A finite revision model passed 73 checks with fixed inputs (0 failed); three model defects were found and fixed during preparation. In one observation of a file operation, a separate copy failed finalisation in a previous update (301 of 302 save operations succeeded) and the service gave no cause; the full archive still matched the canonical sources (348 of 348 hashes). No real distributed backend, authentication, books or classifier were used, and 36 subject and load setups remain planned and not executed. Superiority over simply replacing the last record is not shown.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>Seven coordinates are distinguished: existence of content, assessment of its grounds, applicability, normative acceptance, package publication, choice of current state and completion of delivery. Success on one does not change another. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment; seven is not claimed necessary.</li><li>The finite machine passed 73 checks: 24 authored vectors, 39 negative controls, 5 finite enumerations and 5 positive checks. Basis type: finite-test. The count 73 and the 66 configurations use different units.</li><li>Three defects of the first model version were found by the authors and fixed: a boolean accepted as an integer receipt generation, a receipt confirmed without an observed publication effect, and the path <code>.</code> accepted as a manifest member. A second agent reviewed 12 boundary observations and found no new blocking defects; this is not expert review. Basis type: finite-test.</li><li>In the single R0015 observation, one separate copy stayed at an old version while the archive was intact; the cause was not disclosed. The audit shows 301 of 302 saves and 348 of 348 hashes. Basis type: finite-test; one operation, not repeated; the revision model (MM_A0364) was NOT read.</li><li>Dependency analysis distinguishes AND/OR structures of sufficient grounds. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment; completeness of dependency discovery was not measured.</li><li>The RU10 cross-check (kit authors, one assistant) is partly verified: the r1 report confirms two rejected packaging attempts, a first-adapter defect (empty <code>Blueprint</code> list) and an unrebuilt knowledge package. Retention of R0 history is not verified from the open reports. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>Authentication and atomic external storage are assumptions, not results.</li><li>Real acceptance, deployment and rollback of a contract registry were not run; mass revision of a whole base and an external server current head were not tested.</li><li>Results of the 36 planned setups are absent, as are 9 sequential reviews. Four hypotheses (separated states, typed dependencies, partial-publication reconciliation, versioned canon) are untested.</li><li>Two numbers from different instruments (786/12 and 772/0) are not comparable; the qualification report MM_A10474 was not read.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>Not integrated and still missing: the NAV reports, the TIM reports, MM_OBLIGATIONS_20261030 together with the previous-stage report, the runs behind section 7 of the knowledge-admission amendment (MM_KA0004), and the items ING-01 to ING-08.</li><li>The crosswalk content is a one-assistant self-check, not independent confirmation.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>The Russian full text is the terminology edition of 2026-11-03 (front matter, links aside). Its opening paragraph omits executed results and first failures; this page follows the corrected wording of the editorial review. The Russian text is published without the card corrections, so its abstract may differ from this page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/P10_revision_and_canon.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P10_revision_and_canon.md","image":"knowledge-landscape.webp","source_sha256":"02bde45b44618d2bfc9b2e7dcf93ad697458f3091c8882ed68875d2ffd8be1f7"},{"id":"p11","kind":"paper","filename":"P11_evaluation_and_falsification.md","title":"Evaluation, Counterexamples and the Limits of Claims","titleRu":"Проверка, контрпримеры и границы утверждений","artifact":"MM_A0208","revision":"MM_A0208-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"The paper proposes a programme for testing meaning management as a whole process, from request to observable result and back-tracing. The scientific question is whether explicit meaning objects, conditions, dependencies and provenance help a person or a model reach a better-grounded result under limited source access and budget. The question is not answered on a representative or independent load: local targeted comparisons against a strong flat implementation gave equal statuses and no established superiority. An appendix keeps runs R37-R44, including first failures.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0208 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0208-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P11_evaluation_and_falsification.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>The paper proposes a programme for testing meaning management as a whole process, from request to observable result and back-tracing. The scientific question is whether explicit meaning objects, conditions, dependencies and provenance help a person or a model reach a better-grounded result under limited source access and budget. The question is not answered on a representative or independent load: local targeted comparisons against a strong flat implementation gave equal statuses and no established superiority. An appendix keeps runs R37-R44, including first failures.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>The six hypotheses in the paper&#x27;s table remain hypotheses, with no comparison on a representative or independent load. Basis type: hypothesis.</li><li>R42: equal statuses in 30 of 30 pairs with a shared validator, so not independent. The first R44 integration checks gave 15 of 16 expected outcomes; not replaced by 16 of 16. Basis type: finite-test.</li><li>R43 (8 pairs) and R44 (5 task pairs and 24 projections) also gave equal statuses; none is representative or independent. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment.</li><li>Eight verification subjects and three separate coverage reports are design decisions. No observations on real users exist; for agents only limited local model answers (R43: 16, R44: 10; not blind). Basis type: authors-domain-assessment.</li><li>Preservation of obligations under exact reuse holds only for immutable content, matching requirements and passed admission checks. The justification is not reproduced in this paper; the mapping of the row to a specific I15 property is NOT VERIFIED; the source MM_A0457 was not read by the card writer (the reuse model is MM_A0459). Basis type: proof-under-premises.</li><li>A cross-check by the kit authors, self-checked by one assistant and not independent, links separate conformance, source-fidelity, outcome and limit checks to 40 of 40 expected outcomes; the first harness run gave 31 of 32. It is not held-out and has no blind review. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>The catalogue of 320 synthetic plans and 18 prepared illustrations (the 18 not re-derived, source not read) is not a sample of solved tasks.</li><li>Results on well-known books cannot exclude prior model exposure; the cited contamination work was not read (NOT VERIFIED).</li><li>The related reuse pilot (median latency ratio 0.9982, no stable gain) did not compare a compilation level with an exact-match cache, so that falsification criterion is not yet applied.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open; it still needs the formal-properties document (MM_A0457) behind the reuse row.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>This English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>Not integrated and still missing: the NAV reports, the TIM reports, MM_OBLIGATIONS_20261030 together with the previous-stage report, the runs behind section 7 of the knowledge-admission amendment (MM_KA0004), and the items ING-01 to ING-08.</li><li>Held inconsistency: one corpus audit appears as 5 594 flags and 169 ledger rows, and elsewhere as 5 538 flags and 174 ledger edits; unexplained.</li><li>Editorial notes read the R44 task comparison as 5 task pairs and 24 projections, and the 51 equivalent A/B pairs of the same section as qualification control inputs, not a task comparison. The Russian text as published still lists 51 A/B pairs next to the comparison and is unchanged.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>The Russian full text is the terminology edition of 2026-11-03. The late synthesis row is integrated only as the authors&#x27; self-check. The Russian text is published without the card corrections, so its abstract may differ from this page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/P11_evaluation_and_falsification.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P11_evaluation_and_falsification.md","image":"knowledge-dialogue.webp","source_sha256":"c390c8e278e254cffda1237483cb66caadcf1156a7c72dbe2742986f544a5cc7"},{"id":"p12","kind":"paper","filename":"P12_compilation_caching_and_reuse.md","title":"Knowledge Compilation: Preparing Results and the Admissibility of Reuse","titleRu":"Компиляция знания: подготовка результатов и допустимость повторного использования","artifact":"MM_A0209","revision":"MM_A0209-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"The paper treats reuse of prepared results of extraction, retrieval, composition and professional preparation as a separate admission operation. Reusing a prepared result requires a match with the new request, current constraints, required grounds and the recipient's profile. The paper formalises this boundary and states conditional properties, an economic formulation, strong alternatives and grounds for refutation. The outcome is a research model and a finite executable profile. Effectiveness on real books, causal usefulness and industrial correctness remain hypotheses. The one measured efficiency result, a local paired pilot, found no stable gain.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0209 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0209-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P12_compilation_caching_and_reuse.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>The paper treats reuse of prepared results of extraction, retrieval, composition and professional preparation as a separate admission operation. Reusing a prepared result requires a match with the new request, current constraints, required grounds and the recipient&#x27;s profile. The paper formalises this boundary and states conditional properties, an economic formulation, strong alternatives and grounds for refutation. The outcome is a research model and a finite executable profile. Effectiveness on real books, causal usefulness and industrial correctness remain hypotheses. The one measured efficiency result, a local paired pilot, found no stable gain.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>The central question has two halves: admissibility of carrying a result between requests, which admits conditional proofs, and efficiency at full cost, which stays a hypothesis. Basis type: hypothesis.</li><li>Main conditional property: if the checked properties are finite, the dependency set contains every input affecting them, and the transformation preserves them, they hold after reuse. It is a conditional lemma with a justification and a finite model check, not a mechanised proof; the justification was not read (NOT VERIFIED), and completeness for real content is not claimed. Basis type: proof-under-premises.</li><li>Local exact-versus-off pilot: three pairs, 144 measured requests each, 432 exact-mode reads; latency ratios 1.0185, 0.9982, 0.8017; median 0.9982. No stable gain; no semantic compiler or model, so no token or compilation saving. Basis type: finite-test.</li><li>In R42 all 60 executions matched expected outcomes and no listed violation occurred, yet 36 assessments kept an unresolved mapping and 12 an unknown new condition. The simple branch equalled the graph branch in all 30 cases, with a shared validator. A synthetic cost example gives 10000 versus 1740 units with break-even at N=18; a second example gives a loss of 10849; the executable example (MM_A0453) was not read and 10849 could not be reproduced from the paper&#x27;s parameters. Basis type: finite-test.</li><li>The contribution is a problem formulation; novelty of the integration is not established. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment.</li><li>A later cross-check by the kit authors, self-checked by one assistant and not independent, reports 13 of 14 first text results passing all conditions and 14 of 14 technical replays against knowledge contracts. Context economy is not measured. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>Not established: completeness of dependency manifests for natural language, real error rates, causal usefulness.</li><li>The pilot is one local runtime and did not compare a compilation level with an exact-match cache.</li><li>Untested: harm to rare cases, utility-assessment cost above the gain, false completeness after insertion on real content.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>This English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>Not integrated and still missing: the NAV reports, the TIM reports, MM_OBLIGATIONS_20261030 together with the previous-stage report, the runs behind section 7 of the knowledge-admission amendment (MM_KA0004), and the items ING-01 to ING-08.</li><li>Late synthesis still needs the formal properties document behind the conditional property.</li><li>Also not read by the card writer: MM_A0461, MM_A2712 and MM_A10830 (the R42 measured-result report); claims resting on them keep the card&#x27;s limited wording.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>The Russian full text is the terminology edition of 2026-11-03. The late synthesis row is only an authors&#x27; self-check. The Russian text is published without the card corrections, so its abstract may differ from this page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/P12_compilation_caching_and_reuse.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P12_compilation_caching_and_reuse.md","image":"knowledge-landscape.webp","source_sha256":"4bfa556d7cd63a3b89d6aedf98939b8e761dfcd0cdfa9aae1532a8b286bb95b9"},{"id":"p13","kind":"paper","filename":"P13_knowledge_utility_and_resource_economics.md","title":"Knowledge Utility, the Cost of Meaning Artifacts and Resource Management","titleRu":"Полезность знаний, стоимость смысловых артефактов и управление ресурсами","artifact":"MM_A0446","revision":"MM_A0446-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"The paper proposes a way to link the life cycle of meaning artifacts to observed resource use, conditions of application and results for specific recipients. The object of evaluation is not a universal \"value of a text\" but the contribution of an artifact version to a goal fixed in advance, relative to an explicit alternative. Costs, including those of the evaluation itself, are counted. The paper offers a synthesis and a contract profile, not a value theory. No retention or ranking policy based on conditional utility has been tested on a real load; the appendix holds only local resource observations from runs R38-R44.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0446 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0446-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P13_knowledge_utility_and_resource_economics.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>The paper proposes a way to link the life cycle of meaning artifacts to observed resource use, conditions of application and results for specific recipients. The object of evaluation is not a universal &quot;value of a text&quot; but the contribution of an artifact version to a goal fixed in advance, relative to an explicit alternative. Costs, including those of the evaluation itself, are counted. The paper offers a synthesis and a contract profile, not a value theory. No retention or ranking policy based on conditional utility has been tested on a real load; the appendix holds only local resource observations from runs R38-R44.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>Four levels are separated, from cost incurred to estimated added contribution. A scalar utility is admissible only for a concrete decision with a published conversion policy; no comparison with a vector was run. Causal usefulness was not estimated (NOT VERIFIED against MM_A0428 or the causal literature, not read). Complaint scenarios A to E are constructed and none was executed. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment.</li><li>Central claim: a utility-managed policy improves the cost of a correct result against strong simple alternatives in a given load. No load was studied and no comparison was made. Basis type: hypothesis.</li><li>Graph and simple implementations agreed in 30 of 30 targeted pairs (R42), with no economic advantage. In R39 the raw <code>met</code> sums (193 and 197) count criteria, not fully correct results, and were an unusable denominator. Basis type: finite-test.</li><li>R43 had 8 pairs and 16 answers, and R44 had 5 pairs and 24 projections, with equal results and no economic advantage; neither tests the utility policy. Basis type: hypothesis.</li><li>A later cross-check by the kit authors, self-checked by one assistant and not independent, separates a subject self-check on 14 cases from efficiency. The 14 cases are 15 text versions, not 15 trials. No measured gain, cost, tokens or latency and no matched baseline or blind reviewer are recorded. Basis type: authors-domain-assessment.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>No price of knowledge, causal usefulness or right to payment is established.</li><li>R42 timing includes a shared validator and is not product latency.</li><li>In R43, 7 of 153 non-empty remarks went to limited checking and 146 did not; this is a routing policy, not a proven saving of 146 OCR calls.</li><li>A cheaper flat implementation may exist; this is open.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>This English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>Not integrated and still missing: the NAV reports, the TIM reports, MM_OBLIGATIONS_20261030 together with the previous-stage report, the runs behind section 7 of the knowledge-admission amendment (MM_KA0004), and the items ING-01 to ING-08.</li><li>Late synthesis still needs completion evidence for later cost and quality obligations.</li><li>Not read by the card writer: MM_A5295, MM_A10830 and MM_A11093 (the R39, R42 and R43 records); claims resting on them keep the card&#x27;s limited wording.</li><li>The R44 task comparison here is 5 pairs and 24 projections. The evaluation paper&#x27;s editorial notes read its fifty-one equivalent A/B pairs as qualification control inputs, not a task comparison.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>The Russian full text is the terminology edition of 2026-11-03. The late synthesis row is only an authors&#x27; self-check. The Russian text is published without the card corrections, so its abstract may differ from this page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/P13_knowledge_utility_and_resource_economics.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/papers/ru/P13_knowledge_utility_and_resource_economics.md","image":"knowledge-landscape.webp","source_sha256":"e94b106209f3822f7e68685f4a653da731d7078e1826f3a37d58d80e7fefb4d8"},{"id":"artifact-registry","kind":"spec","filename":"ARTIFACT_REGISTRY.md","title":"Registry of Shared Artifacts: Identity, Fields and Obligations","titleRu":"Реестр общих артефактов: идентичность, поля и обязанности","artifact":"MM_A0220","revision":"MM_A0220-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"This specification defines a registry of shared artifact types for the Meaning Management model. Registry version 0.1 lists 34 conceptual types: 30 introduced earlier and four added explicitly. A common envelope, `mm-envelope/0.1`, makes an addressable, immutable revision, and profiles set the requirements for each kind of record. The text separates five levels of representation, from artifact type down to physical placement, and defines a four-state value for known, unknown, not-applicable and withheld fields. It declares itself a concept draft that develops toward the draft Knowledge Contract v3 (`3.0.0-draft.1`), and it does not announce a ready API or a completed v3 schema.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0220 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0220-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/ARTIFACT_REGISTRY.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>This specification defines a registry of shared artifact types for the Meaning Management model. Registry version 0.1 lists 34 conceptual types: 30 introduced earlier and four added explicitly. A common envelope, <code>mm-envelope/0.1</code>, makes an addressable, immutable revision, and profiles set the requirements for each kind of record. The text separates five levels of representation, from artifact type down to physical placement, and defines a four-state value for known, unknown, not-applicable and withheld fields. It declares itself a concept draft that develops toward the draft Knowledge Contract v3 (<code>3.0.0-draft.1</code>), and it does not announce a ready API or a completed v3 schema.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>The registry separates five levels: artifact type, representation profile, logical object, immutable revision, and representation or placement. Each level states what it does not imply. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative definition).</li><li>Registry version 0.1 has 34 types, and the common envelope is mandatory in every row. Payload fields are a minimum signature that may be refined. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li><code>KnowledgeValue</code> has four forms: <code>known</code>, <code>unknown</code>, <code>not_applicable</code>, <code>withheld</code>. A value is required only for <code>known</code>; an empty list means known absence in a stated scope; null is not a universal unknown. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li>Immutability applies to a stored revision. A mutable <code>CacheEntry</code> has generations and snapshots, and moving the same copy changes only the placement registry. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li>A local script checks finite records and deliberately damaged variants across four main demonstration groups plus identity checks. The text gives no run counts of its own. Basis type: finite-test (denominator not stated in this text).</li><li>Whether the typed approach beats ordinary versioned metadata, provenance, search and application validators is open. The text says advantage, completeness and universality still need evidence and trials. Basis type: hypothesis.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>Structural correctness of a record does not establish that its content is true, and <code>known</code> means a value is recorded, not independently verified.</li><li>The checking script is not a full JSON Schema or SHACL processor, resolver or extraction system.</li><li>System-level cases remain planned or illustrated; none is reported as observed in operation.</li><li>Reading an envelope does not establish conformance with Knowledge Contract v2 or with the future v3.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>The specification&#x27;s front matter gives status <code>concept_draft</code>, document version 0.2, registry version 0.1.</li><li>Which of the 34 type signatures will survive into v3 is open: the text says future types and carrier may change with justification and migration.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>This page summarises the specification&#x27;s own statements; every rule, number and limit above comes from the Russian text, not from outside material. No separate editorial review wording exists for specifications yet, so no reviewed status wording is applied here.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ARTIFACT_REGISTRY.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/ARTIFACT_REGISTRY.md","image":"knowledge-dialogue.webp","source_sha256":"32bcb0397ffedc1b5f3800a8e51c430dcf7536b66e6de5baaa98d8a74848bee8"},{"id":"cache-identity-and-invalidation","kind":"spec","filename":"CACHE_IDENTITY_AND_INVALIDATION.md","title":"Identity, Dependencies and Invalidation","titleRu":"Идентичность, зависимости и инвалидирование","artifact":"MM_A0221","revision":"MM_A0221-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"This specification sets out how a stored, derived result is addressed, found as a candidate, revised when its basis changes, and admitted for a new delivery. It separates payload identity, build identity, lookup identity and a mutable current head, and treats byte equality, recipe equality, meaning compatibility, sufficiency for a request and authority to deliver as different relations. It also covers negative and top-k results, change events, late workers and restore. The result is a research specification with a finite executable profile; the text states that a real distributed system is not yet implemented.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0221 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0221-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/CACHE_IDENTITY_AND_INVALIDATION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>This specification sets out how a stored, derived result is addressed, found as a candidate, revised when its basis changes, and admitted for a new delivery. It separates payload identity, build identity, lookup identity and a mutable current head, and treats byte equality, recipe equality, meaning compatibility, sufficiency for a request and authority to deliver as different relations. It also covers negative and top-k results, change events, late workers and restore. The result is a research specification with a finite executable profile; the text states that a real distributed system is not yet implemented.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>A hash does not prove origin, truth or a current grant. Digests are compared with algorithm, domain and profile version. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative definition).</li><li>A negative, exhaustive or ranked result carries its scope, predicate, profile, index generation and confirmed observation boundary, since adding a matching object can change the result. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li>The same event ID with the same bytes is handled idempotently; the same ID with different content is a conflict that ends trust in that range until reconciled. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li>If the affected set cannot be proven, a conservative object or scope reset applies; its cost and false revisions are to be measured separately. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li>Under stated premises (complete dependency set, correct oracle, consistent guard, fencing), the model must not allow current publication or delivery that was forbidden before check point L. Basis type: proof-under-premises. Successful examples do not show the premises hold in a real service.</li><li>Minimal checks cover negation and quantifiers, tenants, null versus absence, gaps, lost tail, revocation before TTL, a late worker and restore after revocation; the text gives no counts itself. Basis type: finite-test (denominator not stated in this text).</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>No distributed system is implemented. The finite model assumes a trusted sequential oracle and an atomic check-and-change operation; a distributed transaction, barrier or lease needs separate implementation and analysis.</li><li>A watermark marks a processed boundary in its own scope; it does not prove completeness of subject knowledge.</li><li>After check point L, already-read information is not promised to disappear at the recipient.</li><li>Conformance with RFC 8785 or another external serialisation standard is not claimed from the use of JSON.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>The front matter gives version 1.0, status <code>concept_draft</code>, evidence status <code>research_proposal_with_bounded_executable_profile</code>.</li><li>Publication of sources, index and events under partial failure is handed to a later pass and is not settled here.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>This page summarises the specification&#x27;s own statements; every rule, number and limit above comes from the Russian text, not from outside material. No separate editorial review wording exists for specifications yet, so no reviewed status wording is applied here.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/CACHE_IDENTITY_AND_INVALIDATION.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/CACHE_IDENTITY_AND_INVALIDATION.md","image":"knowledge-landscape.webp","source_sha256":"41a1c33f9655af3f8713bf2cab2c0e4073bfe30d3437c2e8eaa7e505a93c420a"},{"id":"compiled-artifact-contract","kind":"spec","filename":"COMPILED_ARTIFACT_CONTRACT.md","title":"Compiled Artifact Contract","titleRu":"Контракт скомпилированного артефакта","artifact":"MM_A0222","revision":"MM_A0222-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"This specification defines `CompiledArtifact`, a stored derived result of a declared extraction, selection, transformation or assembly of knowledge. It links the result to its representation, build recipe, dependencies, requirements and evidence, so that people and agents can reuse it under stated conditions. It defines a bounded profile, `i16-compiled-artifact/0.1`, with a published JSON Schema and a finite checking program. It adds no new type to the shared registry. The text calls itself a research specification and says the schema and program are not an industrial service or a universal solver of meaning.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0222 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0222-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/COMPILED_ARTIFACT_CONTRACT.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>This specification defines <code>CompiledArtifact</code>, a stored derived result of a declared extraction, selection, transformation or assembly of knowledge. It links the result to its representation, build recipe, dependencies, requirements and evidence, so that people and agents can reuse it under stated conditions. It defines a bounded profile, <code>i16-compiled-artifact/0.1</code>, with a published JSON Schema and a finite checking program. It adds no new type to the shared registry. The text calls itself a research specification and says the schema and program are not an industrial service or a universal solver of meaning.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>Four contracts (<code>CompiledArtifact</code>, <code>BuildRecipe</code>, <code>DependencyManifest</code>, <code>TemplateContract</code>) are existing registry types, and the bounded profile adds no 35th type. A compiled artifact is an immutable revision and does not establish current admission for every recipient. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative definition).</li><li>There are six result kinds (<code>answer</code>, <code>template</code>, <code>context_package</code>, <code>contract_bundle</code>, <code>retrieval_result</code>, <code>dependency_closure</code>), each with a minimum and a forbidden inference; for example, a zero approximate-search result does not prove absence. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li>Coverage is always relative to a pinned requirement set; supported slots and gaps form a disjoint partition of required slots, and <code>no_match</code> needs a declared exhaustive scope. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li>Validation has five levels, from structure to current admission, and success at one level does not establish the next. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li>The text names 16 conditional properties with counterexamples in a separate formal document that this page does not reproduce. Basis type: not-a-claim for this page.</li><li>The migration function returns <code>migration_required</code> with a loss report and creates no target artifact. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>Words such as required and forbidden set rules of this project profile; they do not declare that the external guarantees needed in production are achieved.</li><li>Audio, video, arbitrary graphic formats and arbitrary substitution programs are not declared implemented in 0.1; a PNG example does not show recognition of graphics.</li><li>No production resolver, full migration of old records, or extraction engine exists, and full real books are absent.</li><li>Listing a negative case is not evidence that a test was run; actual runs are reported elsewhere.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>The front matter gives version 1.0, status <code>concept_draft</code>, evidence status <code>proposed_contract_with_bounded_executable_profile</code>.</li><li>Time-to-live policy, final cache keys and the invalidation protocol are handed to later work.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>This page summarises the specification&#x27;s own statements; every rule, number and limit above comes from the Russian text, not from outside material. No separate editorial review wording exists for specifications yet, so no reviewed status wording is applied here.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/COMPILED_ARTIFACT_CONTRACT.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/COMPILED_ARTIFACT_CONTRACT.md","image":"knowledge-landscape.webp","source_sha256":"84ab77c5274bf700551d508fec233596ff06a926dfeb4f292e17945003b1f981"},{"id":"context-package","kind":"spec","filename":"CONTEXT_PACKAGE.md","title":"ContextPackage: Specification and Bounded Executable Profile","titleRu":"ContextPackage: спецификация и ограниченный исполнимый профиль","artifact":"MM_A0223","revision":"MM_A0223-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"This specification defines `ContextPackage`, a versioned package of statements and conditions prepared for one intent and one bounded use. It lets a reader check provenance, coverage, dependencies, scope of applicability and budget. The text lists 13 groups of required fields, a coverage vocabulary, a separate stop-reason vocabulary, and budget and validation rules. It states that it keeps the status of a research proposal. A bounded profile, `i14-context-package/0.1`, defines a finite serialisation, a local recipient and a validator. Successful validation grants no authority to act and does not confirm physical execution.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0223 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0223-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/CONTEXT_PACKAGE.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>This specification defines <code>ContextPackage</code>, a versioned package of statements and conditions prepared for one intent and one bounded use. It lets a reader check provenance, coverage, dependencies, scope of applicability and budget. The text lists 13 groups of required fields, a coverage vocabulary, a separate stop-reason vocabulary, and budget and validation rules. It states that it keeps the status of a research proposal. A bounded profile, <code>i14-context-package/0.1</code>, defines a finite serialisation, a local recipient and a validator. Successful validation grants no authority to act and does not confirm physical execution.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>A package has 13 field groups: identity, intent, snapshot, candidates, selection, dependencies, coverage, exclusions, transformations, evidence, budgets, validation and completion. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative definition).</li><li>Coverage statuses are <code>supported</code>, <code>partial</code>, <code>unsupported</code>, <code>conflicted</code> and <code>unknown</code>; the text calls them a project proposal. Slots of one result are tied to a common subject identity. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li><code>stop_reason</code> has five values (<code>completed</code>, <code>clarification_needed</code>, <code>budget_insufficient</code>, <code>retrieval_limit</code>, <code>stale_evidence</code>) and describes how processing ended, not whether the answer is true. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li>Budget estimates and measurements are stored separately, and required conditions are not trimmed to fit. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li>The bounded profile was executed: 94 of 94 checks passed, comprising 14 positive, 77 negative and three finite enumerations. Only UTF-8 bytes were measured. Basis type: finite-test (94 checks).</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>Model tokenisation, external products and remote delivery were not measured.</li><li>A passing validation does not show that a recipient understood the package, nor a causal contribution of its content.</li><li>A high utility estimate does not allow dropping a unit, a legend or an access right.</li><li>A digest match confirms integrity only against a trusted expected value.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>The front matter gives version 0.4, status <code>concept_draft</code>, evidence status <code>research_proposal_with_bounded_executable_profile</code>.</li><li>Reuse of packages through compilation and caching is handed to later work and is not settled here.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>This page summarises the specification&#x27;s own statements; every rule, number and limit above comes from the Russian text, not from outside material. No separate editorial review wording exists for specifications yet, so no reviewed status wording is applied here.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/CONTEXT_PACKAGE.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/CONTEXT_PACKAGE.md","image":"knowledge-dialogue.webp","source_sha256":"4d9d2d904466a6283535e5b83fb46cf5300629b9b2641de29fcb9e9a63704624"},{"id":"contract-family","kind":"spec","filename":"CONTRACT_FAMILY.md","title":"Family of Contracts for Operations on Meanings and Knowledge","titleRu":"Семейство контрактов операций над смыслами и знаниями","artifact":"MM_A0224","revision":"MM_A0224-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"This specification defines a family of contracts that tie knowledge to the actions allowed on it: preserving a source, extracting meaning, aligning an illustration with text, retrieving, preparing bounded context, handing it over, explaining, doing work, revising and reusing a result. A contract states under which inputs and conditions an operation is admissible, what it keeps and changes, which outcomes are allowed and how they are confirmed. The text defines 17 operation profiles and five outcomes. It declares itself a concept draft (edition 0.9) aligned with the draft Knowledge Contract v3.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0224 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0224-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/CONTRACT_FAMILY.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>This specification defines a family of contracts that tie knowledge to the actions allowed on it: preserving a source, extracting meaning, aligning an illustration with text, retrieving, preparing bounded context, handing it over, explaining, doing work, revising and reusing a result. A contract states under which inputs and conditions an operation is admissible, what it keeps and changes, which outcomes are allowed and how they are confirmed. The text defines 17 operation profiles and five outcomes. It declares itself a concept draft (edition 0.9) aligned with the draft Knowledge Contract v3.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>A contract binds an operation to a version, a scope and a requirements snapshot; structural correctness of a record does not mean its content is true. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative definition).</li><li>There are 17 operation profiles, from Preserve to Reuse. The text says they are a set of possible operations, not seventeen mandatory stages of every request. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li>The five outcomes are success, partial, refused, failed and unresolved. Partial does not pass a success edge automatically. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li>Human and agent recipients receive the same result, conditions, grounds, gaps and next step, in different forms. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li>Practical usefulness of the family is a hypothesis. It must be compared with a good structured summary, ordinary search, graph dependencies and a strong typed workflow at a comparable budget. Negative results are possible. Basis type: hypothesis.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>The historical bounded grammar was checked on authors&#x27; examples only; an industrial executor and a universal predicate solver are not implemented.</li><li>48 planned scenarios, 14 counterexample analyses and six end-to-end routes do not raise the status of 320 earlier items or 18 earlier illustrations.</li><li>The fixture and validator check consistency of authored records; they do not observe a perceptual model at work.</li><li>The practical path covers text and images; audio and video are in the theoretical model only.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>The text gives edition 0.9 and status <code>concept_draft</code>; no front matter is present in the source.</li><li>Compatibility with Knowledge Contract v2 is a migration boundary, not a settled mapping.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>This page summarises the specification&#x27;s own statements; every rule, number and limit above comes from the Russian text, not from outside material. No separate editorial review wording exists for specifications yet, so no reviewed status wording is applied here.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/CONTRACT_FAMILY.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/CONTRACT_FAMILY.md","image":"knowledge-dialogue.webp","source_sha256":"10ce79c47865edf50c06fde36a5e3c49c50b98bb9d547b91a8c1d67a70849b81"},{"id":"knowledge-contract-v3","kind":"spec","filename":"KNOWLEDGE_CONTRACT_V3.md","title":"Knowledge Contract v3: Synthesis Specification","titleRu":"Knowledge Contract v3 — синтез I26","artifact":"MM_A0225","revision":"MM_A0225-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"This specification defines a target design for Knowledge Contract v3 (target identifier `3.0.0-draft.1`): a versioned, bounded package of meaning content for a declared purpose of use. It links typed content to requirements, scope, sources, dependencies, preservation obligations and observations. The text describes nine logical groups, six selective profiles, separate validation levels, and a limited migration of a six-field legacy subset. A concrete carrier, `kc-synthesis/0.1`, is covered only within its own stated scope.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0225 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0225-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/KNOWLEDGE_CONTRACT_V3.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>This specification defines a target design for Knowledge Contract v3 (target identifier <code>3.0.0-draft.1</code>): a versioned, bounded package of meaning content for a declared purpose of use. It links typed content to requirements, scope, sources, dependencies, preservation obligations and observations. The text describes nine logical groups, six selective profiles, separate validation levels, and a limited migration of a six-field legacy subset. A concrete carrier, <code>kc-synthesis/0.1</code>, is covered only within its own stated scope.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>A contract is a versioned package for a declared purpose; its content type is preserved (an extracted instruction is not an accepted norm). Basis type: not-a-claim (normative definition).</li><li>Core instance: nine logical groups, with unknown scope kept distinct from &quot;known to be absent&quot;; profiles are a separate extension container, and an unknown required profile blocks application. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative rules).</li><li>Structural validation, reference and obligation checks, and application assessment against supplied context are separate levels; a positive result does not establish source truth, real fulfilment of a requirement, or authenticity of evidence. Basis type: not-a-claim (scope statement).</li><li>Finite executed checks on the carrier: the first author run passed 35 of 35 ordinary scenarios, and a separate in-team challenge run passed 26 of 26 (six valid positives, seventeen correct refusals, three migration checks). Basis type: finite-test.</li><li>In the same runs, two author stress inputs and four challenge stress inputs with falsely trusted markup were accepted by the model; they are excluded from the conformance share and mark a limit of source admission. Basis type: finite-test (negative result).</li><li>An exploratory strong plain-text form matched the contract on the shared area (9 of 9 each: three admissions, six refusals). Superiority is not established; the comparison was not preregistered and does not measure cost. Basis type: finite-test.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>Real professional work, source truth and general usefulness are not confirmed here.</li><li>Coverage checks test presence of a requirement unit, not actual fulfilment; visual checks test a declared modality, not bytes or legibility; reasoning checks test declared references, not truth of premises.</li><li>The instance revision or digest is not yet bound into attempt and evidence records; global attempt uniqueness, idempotency and observation of real external effects are not implemented.</li><li>The specification does not declare production readiness, a published standard or a finished serialisation, and migration does not claim semantic equivalence or lossless round trips.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>Open by the specification&#x27;s own account: full binding of the instance to execution and acceptance, and privacy filtering of diagnostics.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>This page summarises the specification&#x27;s own statements; it adds no claims. The full text is a draft whose own front matter marks it <code>concept_draft</code>. No separate editorial review wording exists for specifications yet.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/KNOWLEDGE_CONTRACT_V3.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/KNOWLEDGE_CONTRACT_V3.md","image":"knowledge-landscape.webp","source_sha256":"1053856f569e5cc765f7bc65c2bc9c6ec9029e97606f367767fe9a74c8877e2d"},{"id":"knowledge-evolution-contract","kind":"spec","filename":"KNOWLEDGE_EVOLUTION_CONTRACT.md","title":"Knowledge Bases and Contract Evolution","titleRu":"Версии оснований знания и эволюция контрактов","artifact":"MM_A0960","revision":"MM_A0960-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"This specification states a requirement for recording which versions of contracts, profiles and rules a knowledge or decision card was created under, and for handling later change. A card keeps the exact versions used at creation; checks against newer rules are recorded separately, and provenance and earlier revisions are never rewritten. The text defines version layers, creation and change records, an impact graph, a review process and a proposed metadata profile with a local validator. It states that the contract family does not yet have approved production schemas, so the document sets requirements and a bounded profile only.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0960 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0960-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/KNOWLEDGE_EVOLUTION_CONTRACT.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft; the specification states its own status as <code>normative_architecture_requirement_with_proposed_metadata_profile</code>; not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>This specification states a requirement for recording which versions of contracts, profiles and rules a knowledge or decision card was created under, and for handling later change. A card keeps the exact versions used at creation; checks against newer rules are recorded separately, and provenance and earlier revisions are never rewritten. The text defines version layers, creation and change records, an impact graph, a review process and a proposed metadata profile with a local validator. It states that the contract family does not yet have approved production schemas, so the document sets requirements and a bounded profile only.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>Every new card keeps the exact versions of the contracts, profiles and rules used at creation; a later check under new rules is a separate record. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative requirement).</li><li>A new rule version can make an old card incomplete for a given use without making its content false; the result of reassessment is a local value (<code>current_compatible</code>, <code>restricted</code>, <code>requires_review</code>, <code>blocked</code>, <code>unknown</code>) mapped onto existing status axes. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative definition).</li><li>Creation versions may be <code>pinned</code>, <code>not_applicable</code> or <code>unknown</code>; <code>unknown</code> is allowed only for an explicitly marked legacy import, and substituting the current version for an unknown one is forbidden. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative rule).</li><li>The local metadata validator checks finite properties only: pin form, no <code>unknown</code> for a new card, a required meaning-management pin, addressed review links, unique domain profiles, unchanged creation metadata for one card revision, and preserved review-history prefix. Basis type: finite-test (synthetic examples; the text names 24 examples plus eight separately written probes).</li><li>A first failure is kept visible: the initial 0.1 proposal forbade <code>latest</code> only for contract pins, an independent check showed <code>latest</code> accepted in two revision fields, and revision 0.2 fixed this. The text calls this a specific repair, not proof of immutability, and not a held-out test. Basis type: finite-test (negative result, then fix).</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>The validator does not establish authenticity of recorded provenance, truth of knowledge, real compatibility of contracts, completeness of the impact graph, or current rights.</li><li>The example contract documents are fictional, not published versions of any contract.</li><li>Real registries, community changes and server migration keep separate acceptance conditions.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>The specification gives its status as a normative architecture requirement with a proposed metadata profile (version 0.2), not as a published standard.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>This page summarises the specification&#x27;s own statements. Its own status wording is given in the status row above. No separate editorial review wording exists for specifications yet.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/KNOWLEDGE_EVOLUTION_CONTRACT.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/KNOWLEDGE_EVOLUTION_CONTRACT.md","image":"knowledge-dialogue.webp","source_sha256":"6f3be11fc914711cef32f32515d1e774f8a916542903c09b542e975e05f53598"},{"id":"reuse-policy","kind":"spec","filename":"REUSE_POLICY.md","title":"Policy for Permissible Reuse","titleRu":"Политика допустимого повторного использования","artifact":"MM_A0226","revision":"MM_A0226-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"This specification (version 1.0) defines a temporal policy for when a previously prepared knowledge result may be reused. The policy is relative to a concrete request, recipient, artifact revision and accepted rule version. It names three time modes (`strict_current`, `historical_pinned`, `bounded_stale`), defines soft and hard deadlines computed from the last sufficient check, and sets a priority order in which prohibitions and current access come before cost savings. The evidence status is stated as a proposed policy with a bounded executable profile.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0226 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0226-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/REUSE_POLICY.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>This specification (version 1.0) defines a temporal policy for when a previously prepared knowledge result may be reused. The policy is relative to a concrete request, recipient, artifact revision and accepted rule version. It names three time modes (<code>strict_current</code>, <code>historical_pinned</code>, <code>bounded_stale</code>), defines soft and hard deadlines computed from the last sufficient check, and sets a priority order in which prohibitions and current access come before cost savings. The evidence status is stated as a proposed policy with a bounded executable profile.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>Order of checks: prohibitions and current access, then material conditions, result requirements, permissible transformations, time mode, budget, and economic benefit last; saving never cancels earlier obligations. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative rule).</li><li>Three time modes are distinguished, and an unexpired TTL is not proof that nothing changed. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative definition).</li><li>Deadlines count from the last sufficient check, not from the last read; the minimum of applicable deadlines and the request limit applies; a missing deadline is not permission. Issuance on the old basis is allowed only while the upper time bound is strictly below the effective hard deadline, so equality means the window is closed. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative rule).</li><li>Check scenarios are given for a synthetic answer profile (soft 300 s, hard 900 s): access at 100 s and 200 s does not move deadlines, a dependency expiring at 250 s limits issuance, a hard revocation at 120 s stops it. The text says these stay <code>planned</code> or <code>illustrated</code> until executed and independently checked. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li>The table of profile durations is a historical illustrative set from draft 0.3. Basis type: hypothesis (starting values for experiments; correctness is subject to experimental checking).</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>No production TTL is established. The listed values are not normative and not derived from production data.</li><li>Passing arithmetic checks does not establish optimality of any TTL or completeness of a dependency manifest.</li><li>Real books, network authorities, clocks, distributed issuance, load and causal savings remain separate checks.</li><li>The policy governs use of knowledge only; it does not authorise a physical action, publishing on a user&#x27;s behalf, or a repeated payment.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>Open by the specification&#x27;s own account: calibration of any numeric candidate, which needs recorded origin, task family, update distribution, quality and cost metrics, and a pilot kept separate from a confirming sample.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>This page summarises the specification&#x27;s own statements; it adds no claims. The full text marks itself <code>concept_draft</code>. No separate editorial review wording exists for specifications yet.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/REUSE_POLICY.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/REUSE_POLICY.md","image":"knowledge-prism.webp","source_sha256":"62ddd1c6b9332de7b06e78a7a071093835b3b303551a0b0cd63d80b61fb2cf5c"},{"id":"semantic-types","kind":"spec","filename":"SEMANTIC_TYPES.md","title":"Content Types and Independent Classification Axes","titleRu":"Типы содержания и независимые оси классификации","artifact":"MM_A0227","revision":"MM_A0227-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"This specification (version 0.7) proposes how to keep apart the differences that matter for search, explanation, document preparation, visual comparison and work execution. It offers ten analytical axes, eight canonical facets of a `MeaningObject`, and a profile for multimodal content. It keeps the 34 general artifact types and the `mm-envelope/0.1` envelope from the artifact registry, and does not add new general types. Practical scope is text and images; audio and video are described only in theory. The text calls the result a working model open to checking and revision.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0227 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0227-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/SEMANTIC_TYPES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>This specification (version 0.7) proposes how to keep apart the differences that matter for search, explanation, document preparation, visual comparison and work execution. It offers ten analytical axes, eight canonical facets of a <code>MeaningObject</code>, and a profile for multimodal content. It keeps the 34 general artifact types and the <code>mm-envelope/0.1</code> envelope from the artifact registry, and does not add new general types. Practical scope is text and images; audio and video are described only in theory. The text calls the result a working model open to checking and revision.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>One tree of knowledge kinds is insufficient: a figure can describe a device, show an error and quote someone else&#x27;s solution. Basis type: not-a-claim (design rationale).</li><li>The ten axes are listed with canonical placement of eight facets (<code>content_kinds</code>, <code>discourse_functions</code>, <code>aboutness</code>, <code>source_position</code>, <code>semantic_operators</code>, <code>assessment_refs</code>, <code>governance_refs</code>, plus representation modes), attribution as a record, and application scope as a view. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative definition).</li><li>Independence of axes means separate responsibility of fields and a ban on unjustified transitions; it is not statistical independence. Basis type: not-a-claim.</li><li>Missing information is expressed as <code>unknown</code>, <code>not_applicable</code> or <code>withheld</code> with a reason, never as an empty list; an empty <code>authority_refs</code> does not confirm permission to act. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative rule).</li><li>Checks run on finite synthetic fixtures for limited structural properties only; the text states this is not a machine-learning or vision-model run, not an annotator study and not processing of three books. Basis type: finite-test (no denominator is given in the specification text itself).</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>An exhaustive classification of all meanings is not proven; the number of axes is not claimed to be correct.</li><li>Success in structural checks does not establish reference resolution, extraction correctness, faithfulness to the source, interpretation, sufficiency or action results; OCR quality is not carried over to topology.</li><li>A conditional proof of requirement preservation holds only for a known sufficient protected set and does not prove completeness of a wrongly assembled set.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>Open by the specification&#x27;s own account: a future trial must fix the corpus, instructions, vocabularies, references and metrics before evaluation, separate tuning from control, and compare against good OCR, captions and plain page transfer.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>This page summarises the specification&#x27;s own statements; it adds no claims. The full text marks itself <code>concept_draft</code>. No separate editorial review wording exists for specifications yet.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/SEMANTIC_TYPES.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/SEMANTIC_TYPES.md","image":"knowledge-landscape.webp","source_sha256":"a378559d1847ec9343d4725773da40a817634413b35edcdc56b6f3b756c82279"},{"id":"status-model","kind":"spec","filename":"STATUS_MODEL.md","title":"Independent Statuses, Assessment Scopes and Transitions","titleRu":"Независимые статусы, области оценки и переходы","artifact":"MM_A0228","revision":"MM_A0228-entry-en-r1","status":"scientific draft","summary":"This specification (model version `status-model/0.1`) argues that a single global label such as \"ready\", \"valid\" or \"reliable\" is insufficient, because it mixes presence of data, semantic support, execution, external effects, currency and scientific status. It introduces 22 independent axes with addressable observations and rules for change, and describes several of them: coverage of a request, run phase and outcome, stop reason, effect observation, check result, research status, case status and data origin. The text calls itself a design model, not a ready industrial schema.","html":"<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Source metadata\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Artifact id</td><td>MM_A0228 (permanent)</td></tr><tr><td>Entry page revision</td><td>MM_A0228-entry-en-r1</td></tr><tr><td>Full text</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/STATUS_MODEL.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Russian original</a>, language: Russian</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>scientific draft (<code>concept_draft</code>); not a finished result</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n<p>This specification (model version <code>status-model/0.1</code>) argues that a single global label such as &quot;ready&quot;, &quot;valid&quot; or &quot;reliable&quot; is insufficient, because it mixes presence of data, semantic support, execution, external effects, currency and scientific status. It introduces 22 independent axes with addressable observations and rules for change, and describes several of them: coverage of a request, run phase and outcome, stop reason, effect observation, check result, research status, case status and data origin. The text calls itself a design model, not a ready industrial schema.</p>\n<h2 id=\"claims-and-their-basis\">Claims and their basis</h2>\n<ul><li>A single global status is insufficient; statuses are separate axes, each relative to pinned requirements, target, scope and snapshot. Basis type: not-a-claim (design rationale and normative definition).</li><li>Coverage uses <code>supported</code>, <code>partial</code>, <code>unsupported</code>, <code>conflicted</code> and <code>unknown</code>; coverage reports are addressed separately per stage (candidate set, context package, output), because assembly may drop found conditions. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative definition).</li><li>Operation outcome, stop reason, effect observation and check result are different things: <code>finished</code> does not settle the fate of a remote action, <code>failed</code> does not mean rollback. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative rules).</li><li>Research status keeps the vocabulary <code>concept_draft</code>, <code>protocol_frozen</code>, <code>results_available</code>, <code>reviewed</code>, with a required scope; <code>reviewed</code> requires references to author, subject, method and conclusion. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative rule).</li><li>Case status uses <code>planned</code>, <code>illustrated</code>, <code>executed</code>, <code>validated</code>; a failed run still counts as executed, and an illustration on an artificial fragment does not confirm work on a real book. The text states that 320 cases remain <code>planned</code> and 18 general examples are illustrations. Basis type: not-a-claim (status statement with stated counts).</li><li>A public claim of a supported scenario must name profile, scope, inputs, limits, system version, protocol and the actual type of evidence; a document status or a passing structural validator does not support a claim that a system works. Basis type: not-a-claim (normative rule).</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"limits\">Limits</h2>\n<ul><li>The model is not a finished industrial schema and does not itself establish any result for a system.</li><li>The old <code>validation_status</code> field is kept only as a short field for early illustrations; a bare <code>passed</code> without a subject does not show contract suitability.</li><li>Local finite checks described in the text do not replace system trials or checks on real material.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"status-and-what-is-open\">Status and what is open</h2>\n<ul><li>The late research synthesis gate is open.</li><li>Independent semantic review of this text has not been performed.</li><li>The English page is a summary, not a translation, and does not replace the Russian original.</li><li>Open by the specification&#x27;s own account: planned system trials remain planned, and real-book cases are not executed.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"relation-to-the-full-text\">Relation to the full text</h2>\n<p>This page summarises the specification&#x27;s own statements; it adds no claims. The full text marks itself <code>concept_draft</code>. No separate editorial review wording exists for specifications yet.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credit-and-licence\">Credit and licence</h2>\n<p>Based on Knowledge Contract Arcana, <a href=\"https://contract.place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://contract.place</a> (CC BY 4.0). Licence: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>. Credit lines and how to cite: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ATTRIBUTION.md</a>; rights holder statement for the repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/NOTICE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOTICE</a>; third-party sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCES.md</a>.</p>","source":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/STATUS_MODEL.md","russian":"https://github.com/Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract/blob/main/spec/ru/STATUS_MODEL.md","image":"knowledge-dialogue.webp","source_sha256":"90077c0e2542debe9bac7a3729de6205a17c1a8e6901cdc84e3178430f352bd9"}],"articles":[{"abstract":"The available sources are heterogeneous: queries, search results, memory, instructions, tools, Policy, and model assumptions together form the available context, yet they do not automatically determine which task-specific semantic commitment has been selected, how it was issued, what realizes it, or whether a particular action is permitted.\n\nThe central contribution is Meaning Management as an architectural layer governing the lifecycle of task-specific semantic commitments. The selection is fixed by a Resolution Receipt; the Knowledge Contract is separated from issuance; post-issuance Binding is separated from the current Authorization. Variant A, the BKG, the Resolver, the identity model, Expansion/Evolution, and the execution gate formally specify the mechanisms that support this decomposition.\n\nThe surveyed purposive corpus covers prompting, retrieval, memory, orchestration, provenance, workflows, policy evaluation, and knowledge representation individually, but provides no single model of this governed transition; the finding is bounded by the corpus and asserts no historical priority. Practical usefulness is tested by nine hypotheses and nine protocols, HYP/EXP-001–009. The experiments have not been run, so error reduction, improved diagnosis, and acceptable cost are not demonstrated.","description":"A conceptual architecture that separates available context, selected semantic commitments, the immutable Knowledge Contract, runtime binding, and the authorization of a particular action.","image":"architecture-original.jpg","source":"https://arcanada.ai/en/blog/meaning-management-knowledge-contract-architecture","status":"The Status of This Publication\n\nResearch 17 — Russian Semantic Source v1 Frozen. The canonical Russian version of the conceptual architecture and the preregistration specification. Empirical validation of the architecture has not yet been performed.\n\nDOI: 10.5281/zenodo.22013923 — the English preprint is deposited in Zenodo (CERN) under CC BY 4.0. Please cite the DOI.\n\nThis status does not imply a finished implementation, a proven superiority, or production readiness. This English text is a translation of the frozen Russian source through the shared Arcanada glossary, not an independent academic rewrite.","title":"Meaning Management in Autonomous AI Systems: the Knowledge Contract Architecture","id":"knowledge-contract-architecture"},{"abstract":"Systems of cooperating LLM agents exchange state as prose. Prose handoffs lose deontic force, invert relation directions, invite readers to fill gaps with defaults, and leave a knowledge store’s internal wholeness uncheckable. We present a knowledge substrate in which the unit of exchange is a context — a finite set of typed, scoped assertions under a snapshot pin — carried on immutable, digest-pinned, append-only revisions, with every algebraic law of the transfer operations proved or refuted on this carrier rather than assumed. The substrate is implemented and mutation-tested — a refusal catalog of 27 codes at the 2026-08-30 evidence pin, each proven red and growing since only through that same door (§8.10); sixteen invariants enforced at honestly labeled tiers; the reduction ladder R0–R3 with exactness certificates — and exercised on real work: a live store grown from 14 to 134 revisions at the §8.10 recount — organic dogfooding for the first stretch, then a bulk corpus lift (14→63, §8.8) and requirements work this paper does not describe (63→134, §8.10), named as what each stretch was rather than folded under one word (an adversarial review, 2026-09-09, found “dogfooding” over-general for growth this paper’s own §8.8/§8.10 attribute to two other causes) — an admission gate 4-for-4 on real tasks, two write races decided by the append-only law, and two contour defects the run itself surfaced — a truncating renderer and an ungoverned executor over-claim. The work refutes three of this line’s own claims — two facets of the token-economy claim and one store-debt figure, the last felled by the parallel run rather than the evaluation — and narrows the delta claim; the refutations are the headline result. On a stage-snapshot-dominated corpus — session-to-session handoffs, where the pilot’s largest reductions (43.1%, 36.4%) lived, are excluded from the systematic sample and untested here — automated spec-only encoding inflates tokens 7.6% across 18 samples, while a structured-summary baseline under the same instruction reaches 14.8% losslessly on the same sources: reduction tracks the encoder, not the format, on this frame. Hand encoding lands within 0.1 percentage points of the pilot’s 38% on a 4-sample subset where the automated arm reduces only 2.2% — a single-point match against a pilot whose own per-artifact spread is about 12 points, stated as what it is rather than as reproduction. Recall of load-bearing source units — not fidelity in the full sense; this measure counts survival of what the source stated and cannot see a fabricated addition (§1.1’s second failure class), a limit an adversarial review found unstated (2026-09-09) — measured jointly: automated packets preserve 99.3% of 437 semantic units, but the hand encoding behind the 38% preserved only 82.7% — the token win and the completeness rule trade against each other, and token-matched compression across formats remains unmeasured. The delta claim narrows to within-task chains (4/4 counter-pairs); at near-lossless encoding, 144 blind downstream grades hit a 47/48 ceiling in every arm alike — no test with that little variance has the power to distinguish packet from honest prose, and none is claimed to. What the typed carrier exhibits, uncompared (an adversarial review, 2026-09-09, found “demonstrably earns” overstated — §8.7 item 4): machine-checkable recall of load-bearing source units after the fact — an observed MUST→SHOULD drift caught by the evaluation’s unit audit, checkable because modality is a field, and not a fidelity claim in the sense that would also catch a fabricated addition — admission gating, digest-decided concurrency, and projection focus. The co-evolution objection — that the corpus and its enforcing checks were built together — has two measured limits. A sensitivity replay, run in the store’s own append-only order, finds pre-enforcement source content for 10 of the 15 discriminable refusal codes; for the other 5 the objection stands, tested and unrefuted. A separate check-removal experiment finds three codes whose suppression admits a revision that subsequently crashes the unchanged Markdown renderer, with no pre-enforcement source witness for those three. This establishes necessity for that operation on those inputs, not independence of the corpus or failure of downstream LLM work. For the algebraic laws of §4 and the invariants of §5 the objection is untested — none of Theorem 1, Proposition 5, I4 or I5 is among the 26 codes the earlier 86-code sensitivity replay reached (§8.7 item 9); membership in the current replay’s 31 witnessed codes was not re-checked. What the design is not compared against is named to the same standard rather than conceded in a phrase: retrieval-augmented handoff, standard graph serializations under shape validation, and token-matched baselines are unmeasured, each carrying the result that would falsify the design. The method itself is adapted rather than invented — specification mutation and vacuity detection, credited in §2.10, where the analogy to weak-versus-strong mutation is withdrawn as wrong. A measurement instrument fabricated a number twice; only recomputation-from-source in CI held.\n\nWhat this paper is for, stated so it can be quoted against us: it reports what a typed, digest-pinned substrate for inter-agent knowledge transfer exhibits, uncompared — and the measured answer is refusal, not economy.\n\n","description":"The second version of the Knowledge Contract work: the typed substrate implemented and mutation-tested, its algebraic laws proved or refuted on the carrier, and the empirical check version 1 declared missing — with the refutations as the headline result.","image":"knowledge-v2-original.jpg","source":"https://arcanada.ai/en/blog/meaning-management-knowledge-contract-v2","status":"The Status of This Publication\n\nAuthor: Pavel Valentov — Independent Researcher. ORCID: 0009-0001-2567-4584. No co-authors, affiliations, or funding sources are claimed.\n\nResearch 17 — Version 2. English Semantic Source. The second version of the Knowledge Contract work. Version 1 (frozen 2026-08-14) declared: «Empirical validation of the architecture has not yet been performed.» This version carries that validation: the substrate is implemented and mutation-tested, and the evaluation’s headline results are refutations of this line’s own earlier claims.\n\nPredecessor: Version 1 — DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.22013923 (CC BY 4.0). Version 1 remains frozen and citable; where the two versions disagree, the disagreement is stated here and v1 stands unchanged.\n\nCanonical language: unlike v1 (frozen Russian source, derived English), v2’s source is English; a Russian rendering, if made, derives from this text through the shared Arcanada glossary. This v2 text is not yet deposited on Zenodo; versioning the deposited record is the author’s act. This status does not imply proven superiority or production readiness.","title":"Knowledge Contracts, Version 2: A Typed Substrate for Inter-Agent Knowledge Transfer, with Its Algebraic Laws Proved or Refuted","id":"knowledge-contract-v2"}],"source":"https://contract.place/","license":"CC-BY-4.0","author":"Pavel Valentov","retrieved":"2026-11-04"};
